    "maps-site/index.html sizes the Leaflet map once at startup (fillZoom() reads map.getSize()) and re-measures only on a window resize, so when the web fonts land the header reflows (iPhone 13: 111 px on the fallback serif, 116 px with EB Garamond and Lora) and Leaflet keeps the pre-swap size (iphone13 #map 390x509 vs Leaflet 390x518; pixel7 698 vs 693; landscape 215 vs 218; desktop 688 vs 691; desktop2x 820 vs 823). Fix: one ResizeObserver on #map (document.fonts.ready may also trigger it) that calls map.invalidateSize() and re-runs the existing fit (fillZoom) when, and only when, the #map box changed; created once, never a loop, no timer",
    "after load, on all five profiles, Leaflet's getSize() equals the #map box (the capture runs with the production fonts answered after the startup layout, as R1 was, so the swap happens after the first fit and the re-fit is exercised)",
